
This project proposes a digital solutions to promote fair pricing, transparency, and efficient food delivery systems across African markets. Food vending is a major source of livelihood and daily food supply in Africa. Despite its importance, the sector is affected by price manipulation, poor transparency, inconsistent food quality, and unreliable delivery services. Most food vendors operate informally, making regulation and consumer protection difficult. The project will develop a mobile and web-based food marketplace platform with the following features: Vendor registration and verification Standard price listing based on daily market prices Digital weighing and measurement standards Online food ordering system GPS-enabled delivery tracking Multiple digital payment options Customer feedback and rating system Digital transaction history and receipts.For my project idea, I focused on creating a digital solution that can help food vendors connect with customers and improve delivery services in African communities. This kind of system can help vendors reach more customers while making it easier for people to order food from their homes.
Food vendors and delivery services in many African communities face the following challenges:-
*Arbitrary price increases and exploitation of consumers.
*Inconsistent measurement of food quantities.
*Lack of transparent pricing information.
*Poor coordination between vendors and delivery agents.
*Delayed deliveries and food spoilage.
*Absence of digital records and accountability.
These issues reduce consumer trust, affect food security, and limit economic growth for honest vendors and farmers.
